{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1497 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "c4323c699ca33e3d1c2992bfd7067c59432d60c7c074201708cd267a1ac2c3f2" :edb/db-before-t 1496 :edb/db-after-t 1497 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534809 50 #inst "2026-10-08T07:40:54.913Z" 13194139534809 true] [17592186068768 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311411 13194139534809 true] [17592186068769 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311397 13194139534809 true] [17592186068769 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311425 13194139534809 true] [17592186068769 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311432 13194139534809 true] [17592186068770 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311418 13194139534809 true] [17592186068772 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311390 13194139534809 true] [17592186068772 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311404 13194139534809 true] [17592186068986 1100 "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y^{\\prime } = y\\sin x$ for $y \\ne 0$." 13194139534809 false] [17592186068986 1100 "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" 13194139534809 true] [17592186068986 1145 "Because $y\\ne0$, separate and integrate:\n$$\\frac{dy}{y}=\\sin x\\,dx,\\qquad \\ln|y|=-\\cos x+C.$$\nExponentiating and absorbing the sign into a nonzero constant gives $y=Ke^{-\\cos x}$, with $K\\ne0$." 13194139534809 false] [17592186068986 1145 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311390 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311391 13194139534809 true] [17592186311390 1089 "q-118885" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311390 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534809 true] [17592186311390 1100 "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}{cos}^{2}⁡y$ for $0<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311390 1113 #uuid "f6a01c34-9b8c-5742-a002-5656bbb5e9ee" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311390 1145 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}{cos}^{2}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡y & ={e}^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C.\n$$" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311392 13194139534809 true] [17592186311391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311393 13194139534809 true] [17592186311391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311394 13194139534809 true] [17592186311391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311395 13194139534809 true] [17592186311391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311396 13194139534809 true] [17592186311391 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534809 true] [17592186311391 1041 "selection" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311391 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311395 13194139534809 true] [17592186311391 1110 #uuid "a3226a4d-2e16-5c47-adc4-39cfe15f3aad" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311392 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{2x}+C" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311392 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311392 1111 #uuid "f82833d6-76e7-526f-8690-513b935ffc80" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311393 1034 "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311393 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311393 1111 #uuid "ab3e08a0-05d6-5f27-be05-eb7635d17b5a" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311394 1034 "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{2x}+C" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311394 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311394 1111 #uuid "28ea0db4-a307-51b9-8d43-26c6d713de6d" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311395 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311395 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311395 1111 #uuid "534e3799-1c4d-5051-a2f0-cee6bd143819" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311396 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=2{e}^{x}+C" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311396 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311396 1111 #uuid "08b86fa1-74c1-52ae-9d88-a7f80bc9f7e6" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311397 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311398 13194139534809 true] [17592186311397 1089 "q-14247" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311397 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534809 true] [17592186311397 1100 "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y+3y{x}^{2}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311397 1113 #uuid "321b7d69-9883-59b2-a4d0-4ebf210bb530" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311397 1145 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y+3y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y+3y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(1+3{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1+3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1+3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =x+{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{3}+x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+x+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}.\n$$" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311399 13194139534809 true] [17592186311398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311400 13194139534809 true] [17592186311398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311401 13194139534809 true] [17592186311398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311402 13194139534809 true] [17592186311398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311403 13194139534809 true] [17592186311398 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534809 true] [17592186311398 1041 "selection" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311398 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311400 13194139534809 true] [17592186311398 1110 #uuid "f6725044-65b4-5d9c-9e33-f0f0efa45de9" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311399 1034 "y=K{e}^{3{x}^{2}+x}" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311399 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311399 1111 #uuid "a2398db1-88c9-574c-91fa-70c569652e09" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311400 1034 "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311400 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311400 1111 #uuid "5415f72f-9dd4-53d1-8dc6-09655c362101" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311401 1034 "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2}}" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311401 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311401 1111 #uuid "3e44b657-91bd-589b-a1d1-611d26d8f603" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311402 1034 "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+x}}" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311402 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311402 1111 #uuid "1c36ba58-cea6-5f95-bafc-9814cf59d93a" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311403 1034 "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+2x}" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311403 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311403 1111 #uuid "d22f4e71-4ecc-5851-886f-48f02106a8aa" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311404 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311405 13194139534809 true] [17592186311404 1089 "q-154357" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311404 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534809 true] [17592186311404 1100 "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡y}$ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311404 1113 #uuid "fed70404-5aaf-52d2-8686-4c656a529df4" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311404 1145 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡y} \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡y & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C.\n$$" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311406 13194139534809 true] [17592186311405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311407 13194139534809 true] [17592186311405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311408 13194139534809 true] [17592186311405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311409 13194139534809 true] [17592186311405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311410 13194139534809 true] [17592186311405 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534809 true] [17592186311405 1041 "selection" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311405 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311408 13194139534809 true] [17592186311405 1110 #uuid "52ecedda-ee36-5ee3-93e0-3e3fb3da0ef2" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311406 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x+C" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311406 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311406 1111 #uuid "03daf3fe-5900-5737-94b7-8be50d710f85" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311407 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\sqrt{x}+C" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311407 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311407 1111 #uuid "2d194fc1-1b54-547d-811f-8c77414c1ee5" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311408 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311408 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311408 1111 #uuid "030e2cbd-9d58-5290-b1d9-91417538f250" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311409 1034 "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311409 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311409 1111 #uuid "ec29e029-fed1-5d53-a9e3-813ab000e0f2" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311410 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\sqrt{x}+C" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311410 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311410 1111 #uuid "31493b54-06f9-5e3e-9f8e-15343c3c84f0" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311411 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311412 13194139534809 true] [17592186311411 1089 "q-158017" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311411 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534809 true] [17592186311411 1100 "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311411 1113 #uuid "ac44d433-a7db-5b48-a5c5-fbb14f94435f" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311411 1145 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}.\n$$" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311412 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311413 13194139534809 true] [17592186311412 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311414 13194139534809 true] [17592186311412 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311415 13194139534809 true] [17592186311412 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311416 13194139534809 true] [17592186311412 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311417 13194139534809 true] [17592186311412 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534809 true] [17592186311412 1041 "selection" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311412 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311415 13194139534809 true] [17592186311412 1110 #uuid "9c763e14-0bd0-5572-8ef8-79991bf0d840" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311413 1034 "y={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}+K" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311413 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311413 1111 #uuid "89cb340f-0478-584c-b2ef-13f05abef887" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311414 1034 "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311414 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311414 1111 #uuid "34609bcf-9819-55ba-9ad6-58492df84acb" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311415 1034 "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311415 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311415 1111 #uuid "7c5bca59-1c2d-504d-ba7c-a8b66a6a82eb" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311416 1034 "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}+K" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311416 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311416 1111 #uuid "11a47ba4-f242-5f17-967a-c31ff9f17190" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311417 1034 "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311417 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311417 1111 #uuid "c03d2759-88bd-5b8a-885b-23c829ab9bdb" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311418 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311419 13194139534809 true] [17592186311418 1089 "q-158025" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311418 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534809 true] [17592186311418 1100 "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{y}^{3}}\n$$" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311418 1113 #uuid "ba587f1b-dab3-553a-b4db-544d035b8b45" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311418 1145 "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}\n$$" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311420 13194139534809 true] [17592186311419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311421 13194139534809 true] [17592186311419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311422 13194139534809 true] [17592186311419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311423 13194139534809 true] [17592186311419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311424 13194139534809 true] [17592186311419 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534809 true] [17592186311419 1041 "selection" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311419 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311424 13194139534809 true] [17592186311419 1110 #uuid "5d798e2d-0f06-548c-a16c-b2ee7dde6f1a" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311420 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{3}}{{2}^{x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311420 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311420 1111 #uuid "8c749822-94c7-5c64-8c64-4c6266ddfeb6" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311421 1034 "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311421 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311421 1111 #uuid "564def48-6013-59e6-9baf-190b7104df0e" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311422 1034 "{2}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311422 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311422 1111 #uuid "38df9078-ba5c-5fad-b6cd-04e7a2c8eb0c" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311423 1034 "{2}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311423 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311423 1111 #uuid "5fe54718-6808-5e7a-a523-0f7ed9bb0994" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311424 1034 "{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311424 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311424 1111 #uuid "bb32a9d2-9e67-5063-ab6f-b3b6a29ddb6c" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311425 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311426 13194139534809 true] [17592186311425 1089 "q-3854" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311425 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534809 true] [17592186311425 1100 "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311425 1113 #uuid "c533f957-5ce4-560a-af3f-547368ddc163" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311425 1145 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(2x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}.\n$$" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311427 13194139534809 true] [17592186311426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311428 13194139534809 true] [17592186311426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311429 13194139534809 true] [17592186311426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311430 13194139534809 true] [17592186311426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311431 13194139534809 true] [17592186311426 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534809 true] [17592186311426 1041 "selection" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311426 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311427 13194139534809 true] [17592186311426 1110 #uuid "3d6f149e-7d48-587b-8cb2-9be31ecbf0be" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311427 1034 "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311427 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311427 1111 #uuid "095c386d-e826-5ea2-a5fb-30f72af48e88" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311428 1034 "y={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+K" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311428 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311428 1111 #uuid "ad4aa770-c8f3-5ef3-8ef4-ac28d2806dd4" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311429 1034 "y={e}^{{x}^{2}}+{e}^{{x}^{3}}+K" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311429 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534809 true] [17592186311429 1111 #uuid "f115aba7-d8f5-5d0b-8c18-05b7b59d2bc5" 13194139534809 true] [17592186311430 1034 "y=\\operato